[Music]  archaeologists sure lead exciting lives  you might think that they spend their  days examining old trinkets and writing  dry papers on their findings but that's  really not the case at all instead their  voyage into exotic islands traipsing  through beautiful environments  plundering ancient tombs and fighting  scores of maniacal men at least that's  how Laura props working hours play out  Tomb Raider may have a silly story but  it's so much fun to investigate the  mysterious ruins and kill the many bad  guys they're going to be to absorb decay  still you do have to sit through  cutscenes to bring to life just how poor  the plot is there's a control freak at a  mysterious island - well is after more  control so he's busy replicating ancient  rituals in order to realize his godlike  potential  he's a predictable megalomaniac and the  supporting characters don't light any  fires either  however Laura herself is quite  interesting for voyage from determined  scientist to defeated survivor is  relatable and Ashley becomes stronger  with each new success you grow along  with her her loyalty to her friends is  unwavering as is her commitment to kill  anyone who poses a threat yeah it's a  little unbelievable how quickly she  becomes accustomed to the killing  lifestyle but even though her  development feels a bit rushed she still  feels somewhat real  the fast-moving plot is mitigated by the  slow pacing of your progress Tomb Raider  plops you in huge environments let you  explore at your leisure they're ancient  doodads hidden all over the place and  climbing up walls and walking across  narrow pathways gives you a chance to  relax and admire the many gorgeous  sights  they're also tombs to explore obviously  this is where you have to test Laura's  puzzle-solving abilities you have to  figure out how to reach seemingly  unreachable places and these brief  forays do a great job of giving you  interesting non violent side activities  of course there's still plenty of  fighting Laura moves with speed in the  throws of warfare and movement is  imperative because she can die with only  a few shots blinking behind cover and  then sprinting the higher ground is so  freeing that you find yourself  constantly on the run though you can  hunker down if you prefer just watch out  for fire bombs each fight only lasts a  few minutes so combat never overstays  its welcome and there are lots of  different scenarios to keep you on your  toes  Laura sports the expected assortment of  guns pistols shotguns assault rifles you  know the drill and though firing these  feels perfectly fine the real joy comes  from her bow and arrow  I loved sneaking up on an unsuspecting  fool and then popping him in the head  and then turning my sights on his buddy  before he could sound the alarm and if  your aim is cruel  you can hit them in the knee and then  finish them off with a melee shot yeah  it's dangerous to stay in the open but  it's also so satisfying that it's worth  the risk  but solo adventure stretches on for  dozens of hours if you're striving to  map every collectable which is how I  played and just about every minute is  riveting Laura slowly finds new tools so  you can tear down structures with a rope  bow or blast down doors with a shotgun  this gives you access to more parts the  environments and revisiting past  locations with new powers lets you see  even more of the expansive wall  [Music]  so all the single-player stuff is good  fun but the multiplayer well not quite  don't get me wrong the sharp controls  are just as responsive and there's  undeniable pleasure and hitting someone  in the jaw with an arrow but everything  feels so predictable we've seen  third-person shooters play out like this  before and the lack of surprise leaves  monotony but thankfully multiplayer is  an optional part of an otherwise great  game the definitive edition sports  better textures lighting and other  technical feats from its Xbox 360 and  PlayStation 3 counterparts but that's  besides the point  it's how the cutting-edge tech  complements that fantastic art design  that makes this game look so appealing  and the action is just as enthralling  Tomb Raider is a great reinvention of  this enduring franchise that makes the  eager to see where lore goes in the  future  [Music]  you  [Music]

